# A loop its player keeps going by choice goes on for as long as they choose (CR 104.4b's last sentence): the engine supports
# no shortcut (CR 732.2), the player goes round by hand, and nothing cuts the loop off however many times it comes round. The
# Worldgorger Dragon loop with Bot2's Entombed Ornithopter in a graveyard too: each time Animate Dead enters it chooses what
# it enchants (CR 303.4f), a real choice, and no player is ever made to choose otherwise (docs/rules-exceptions.md, RX-4).
# Bot1 chooses the Dragon forty times and then the Ornithopter, which Animate Dead returns under Bot1's control
# (CR 110.2), and the loop is over. The Dragon stays in Bot1's graveyard; the Swamps are untapped, as the loop returned them.

[Bot1 Deck]
Swamp
Entomb
Animate Dead
Swamp
Swamp
Swamp
Swamp
Worldgorger Dragon
Swamp x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Swamp
Entomb
Island
Island
Island
Island
Island
Island
Ornithopter
Island x10

